    "catalog:tags": "bath, bathtub, bathroom",
    "catalog:note": "Back-to-wall panelled bath, open on the wall side: rim 0.55. Tub 1.52 x 0.56 inside, corners of radius 0.08, 0.43 deep. Walls (box 1.56 x 0.60, y 0.10 to 0.52) and rim (1.70 x 0.70) are each one piece: a cuboid less the tub opening, an outline sweep cut through it. Floor slab 0.02 thick, the opening 0.001 smaller, in the walls. Front and end panels. Two pillar taps 0.10 high, 0.18 apart, at the -x end; faucetMount between them. A mirrored copy keeps the anchors and ports where they are.",
    "catalog:basedOn": "Bath 1.70 x 0.70 x 0.55: drafting standard key dimensions (practice; EN 14516 not read), unverified. Inner corner radius 0.08 generic, unverified. Tap centres 0.18: common UK bath filler centres, no source checked, unverified. Ports: BS EN 12056-2 via the drafting standard, unverified",
    "ifc:class": "IfcSanitaryTerminal",
    "ifc:predefinedType": "BATH",
    "ifcClass": "IfcSanitaryTerminal",
